---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base page="hub" title="Hubs" description="A hub connects your devices to your Conduit from anywhere, without reading anything that passes through it.">
  <div class="wrap hubp">
    <h1>Hubs</h1>
    <p class="lede">Conduit is a protocol, like git. A hub is where your devices meet, like a git host: optional, replaceable, and anyone can run one.</p>

    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h2>What a hub does</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Relays your phone to your computer without opening a port. Traffic is end-to-end encrypted to a key your phone pins from a QR code.</li>
          <li>Stores settings your devices encrypted themselves.</li>
          <li>Lists modules, signed by their authors.</li>
          <li>Serves signed updates.</li>
          <li>Holds accounts and organisations, with email sent through the operator's own provider.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>What it can't do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Read your requests, answers, secrets or settings.</li>
          <li>Pretend to be your computer: your phone checks the computer's key, not the hub's word.</li>
          <li>Push you a module or update that isn't signed by its author or Conduit.</li>
          <li>Keep you: on the same network your phone skips the hub, and you can switch hubs any time.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Three ways to run Conduit</h2>
    <dl class="ways">
      <div><dt>On its own</dt><dd>Everything on one computer, no account anywhere. Phones on the same network can still pair directly.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>With the default hub</dt><dd>Create an account, link your computer with a pairing code, and reach it from anywhere.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>With your own hub</dt><dd>One binary or a Docker Compose file, SQLite or PostgreSQL, your mail provider. Accounts stay on your hub.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/account/">Create an account on this hub</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/docs/self-hosting/">Run your own</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/docs/protocol/hub/">Read the protocol</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .hubp {
    padding-top: 56px;
    max-width: 960px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 44px;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 48px 0 12px;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 20px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 34em;
  }
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 48px;
  }
  .cols ul {
    padding-left: 18px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .ways div {
    padding: 14px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .ways dt {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .ways dd {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
